+    # Verify every requested element independently of the solver's own
+    # convergence test, so a reported success cannot retain a large
+    # trace-element residual.
+    #
+    # The test is stated on the total elemental vector, gas plus condensate,
+    # and only at a level whose solution has no condensed phase. Where a
+    # condensate is present neither reported vector can be compared with the
+    # request: molfracs_atoms_gas is renormalized over the gas alone, so every
+    # element that stays in the gas rises by the fraction that rained out, and
+    # molfracs_atoms keeps the condensate of the previous level whenever the
+    # solve is started from it (use_prev_guess), which leaves the total
+    # carrying atoms the request no longer contains. Measured on the LHS 1140 b
+    # column at He/H = 9: condensate-free levels close to 2e-14 on the total,
+    # the first condensing level to 2e-14 on the total and 9.9e-1 on the gas,
+    # and every level above it to 1.1e+2 on the total and 6e-14 on the gas.
+    # Every level deep enough to set an elemental handoff is condensate-free,
+    # which is where the residual this test exists to catch appears.
+    closure_rtol = max(1.0e-8, 100.0*gas.mass_tol)
+
+    # Compute chemical equilibrium at all altitudes.
+    try:
